{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774723,"nonce":"6xzF6R2O+imTxlVE9lC/9EjiQqs=","title":"ADR-0056 amendment: rerun/retry language + one Pipeline component","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #44 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0056-rerun-retry-language` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-20T10:05:05Z · Merged: 2026-07-20T20:30:23Z\n\nResolves the end-user run-history language left open in the ADR-0056 handoff (a /grill-with-docs session), and implements it end-to-end. Amends ADR-0056; `CONTEXT.md` glossary updated.\n\n- **The run is a timeline.** A step **try** ends `running → succeeded | failed | superseded | cancelled` (+ **shadowed** flag = finished-successful but no longer the of-record latest). \"Take\"/\"attempt\" never surface — the user sees a **row per rerun** and a per-step **tries** strip.\n- **Two \"agains\" split on step state, not who pressed:**\n  - **auto-retry** — engine, a not-yet-succeeded step, same history row, no fork.\n  - **rerun** — the *one* human button; any **terminal** step (failed *or* succeeded); always forks a new version row; cascades downstream; supersedes in-flight descendants.\n  - No separate \"manual retry\" (one control, not two).\n- **superseded** = a try cut short *while running* by a rerun of an ancestor (≠ cancelled = deliberate/no-replacement, ≠ failed). **cascade** = a descendant dragged along by a rerun (attempt-cause, distinct from the rerun target).\n\n- **Read model** (`takes.ts`, all client-side): `cascade` cause; `superseded`/`shadowed` derived from the event log — no engine change, consistent with ADR-0056's \"nothing stored\".\n- **UI**: DAG + step evidence + version-aware Artifacts merge into **one `PIPELINE` component** with an **always-present version dropdown** (rich rows; single version reads \"latest · live\"). Older version → whole component **read-only** (copper edge + banner; Rerun/Cancel/Debug disabled, New run/Debug-pod... New run live). Tries strip labelled by cause (auto-retry / you reran / ⟵ cascade) + outcome (✗ / ⊘ superseded / shadowed). `Restart step` → **Rerun**. Activity stays a separate cross-version log.\n- **Engine** (git-bug `fd6e6d4`): `restart_step` now enqueues a scoped `SUPERSEDE_TEARDOWN` intent for each in-flight descendant it re-arms; `reconcile_supersessions` (driver-side) SIGTERMs exactly those Pods so they don't orphan. The run stays alive.\n\ngit-bug `ca6b530` (read model), `10d346e` (merge component), `b1d9d13` (vocabulary + read-only + verb), `fd6e6d4` (engine teardown) — all done.\n\n- `tsc --noEmit` + `vite build` clean; `cargo check --workspace` clean; engine + 2 new in-memory teardown tests green.\n- **Browser-verified** against a live server's event log (a run with one rerun): version dropdown, rows, read-only snapshot-at-boundary, and the tries vocabulary all render correctly; no console errors.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}